  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `seon.root/wiki-tx` loads the wiki (`seon.docs/load-dir-tx` over the checkout's docs/) onto main in the boot fact's own commit, after the program facts so cited names resolve, and before any agent forks; an unchanged wiki writes nothing. A refused load (a link to no section) is a recorded :platform error naming the link (`my.root/problems` shows it), main keeps the wiki it held, and the boot goes on (`seon.root-test/a-refused-wiki-is-a-recorded-problem-and-the-boot-goes-on`). The declared proof `seon.docs-test/a-booted-root-holds-the-wiki` is not written yet."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.docs/docs-are-data-in-the-store"}
