 {:seon.task/name "a-task-cites-what-it-needs"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists (docs/references.md#sections-in-a-tasks-context): `seon.context/current-state` adds `:sections`: each wiki section a task's plan or instructions cite by `path#anchor`, read from main's sections (`seon.docs/section`) and shown by `seon.docs/view` through `seon.ref/shown` at the citation's depth (a link or one backtick its doc view, three backticks the section whole), one view per address at its strongest depth (`seon.ref/cited`), beside the names the context already resolves (`:references`). Not shown: a whole-page link and a bare prose address (main holds no page entity; the reader keeps a bare word only when it names a file); stored sections have no opening, so only a paragraph lead shows at doc depth. Cut from the first plan: refusing a design with no citations (a proof's job; v1 had none) and a `docs` search function (its own task when an agent needs it)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.docs/docs-are-data-in-the-store"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.context-test/a-task-context-pulls-what-its-plan-cites-at-that-depth}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-wiki-stays-true-and-healthy"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: the wiki's sections on main (`seon.docs/load-tx`), each with the references its text cites (`:seon.section/references`, read by `seon.ref/parse`); there is no docs check yet. Correct: `bin/check docs` is queries over the docs facts, run in every merged-result check, over every page under docs/ plus docs/README.md, AGENTS.md and BAGGAGE.md. Red: a link or `path#anchor` that reaches nothing; a cited path that names no file; any other reference that does not resolve; a stale section, one citing a var at doc or code depth whose defining form differs from the one at the page's last commit (both read with the reader, no text diff). Health is reported first, then red, by these measures (from jolt/patterns 2da2255, `git show 2da2255`, re-keyed from its Describes lines onto code-depth citations): :two-homes (two sections citing one var at code depth: the sections whose `:seon.section/references` hold the var, filtered by the depth `seon.ref/parse` reads from their text), :no-lead, :lead-echoes-heading (the lead's words a subset of the heading's), :lead-too-long (over 40 words), :lead-cites (file:line in the lead), :heading-has-code (a code span or file:line in a heading), :orphan (no link or parent edge reaches it from docs/README.md; a page's sections are reached through the page; README's groups and same-page anchors count as links), :isolated-page (links nowhere), :changelog (a dated heading, or two or more lines starting with a date; a date in prose is not one). Baseline on jolt/wiki's tree: two-homes 20, no-lead 32, lead-cites 18, lead-too-long 5, heading-has-code 14, orphan 13, isolated-page 3. jolt/patterns' three fixture deftests (a-var-with-two-homes-is-duplication-and-names-the-home, a-lead-that-is-missing-echoes-its-heading-runs-long-or-cites-is-flagged, a-heading-with-code-an-orphan-an-isolated-page-and-a-changelog-are-flagged) port with code-depth citations in place of Describes lines. The style is written once, in docs/README.md#how-the-wiki-is-kept."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.docs/docs-are-data-in-the-store"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.docs-test/an-unresolved-reference-is-red
                      seon.docs-test/a-section-older-than-what-it-cites-is-stale
                      seon.docs-test/two-code-depth-homes-are-flagged
                      seon.docs-test/an-orphan-is-flagged}}
 {:seon.task/name "every-concept-has-its-page"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: docs/README.md is the map and states how the wiki is kept (docs/README.md#how-the-wiki-is-kept: one home per concept, the section citing it at code depth; a standalone lead; everything linked; current truth). 19 pages, among them agent, tasks, cost, merging, machine, storage, render, source, references and failure-points. References are what text cites (`seon.ref/parse`, docs/references.md); there are no declared reference keys. Still without a page: root's procs (the system), the checks (bin/check) and the server, whose op table lives in docs/parity.md#the-mcp-server; a task citing them pulls nothing. Source text: jolt/wiki (8da07b4..11f34a1) wrote twelve concept pages, a day older than main and partly untrue on it (`git show jolt/wiki:docs/<page>.md`); main took its rules (README) and rejected its declared keys. Correct, each section verified against main's code before it is written: new pages docs/system.md (one section per proc in resources/seon/system.edn; its idioms stay homed in docs/flow.md and are linked), docs/check.md (bin/check as it runs now; steps as tasks is `seon.reconcile/a-check-step-is-a-task`) and a server page holding the server's one op table; jolt/wiki's store.md folded into docs/storage.md, printer.md and context.md into docs/render.md, program.md into docs/source.md, worktrees.md into docs/merging.md and docs/machine.md, and wiki.md's section shape (plain stable headings with no code, file:line or date; a lead of at most 40 words with no citation; file:line only inside a function) into docs/README.md#how-the-wiki-is-kept. Every page on the map and linking its neighbours, each var's one home citing it at code depth, docs/vocabulary.md linking each word to its section; nothing dated (no session ids, t values, pids, today/still/now). Not applied: Describes lines, `:one`/`:owner`/`:migrate`, `:seon.task/docs`, `:seon.task/refs`, `:seon/docs`, `:pattern-of`, `seon.docs/reached`. Replaces the knowledge held only in AGENTS.md and docstrings for these concepts (AGENTS.md links the pages); retires jolt/wiki and jolt/patterns-wiki-proof. Deletes no code."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.docs/docs-are-data-in-the-store"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.docs-test/the-wiki-loads-with-every-link-resolved
                      seon.docs-test/every-page-is-reached-from-the-map
                      seon.docs-test/every-section-leads-with-a-sentence-of-at-most-40-words}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-proof-a-stub-passes-is-a-placebo"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: nothing detects \"a check that cannot fail\" (AGENTS.md §9) or a proof \"a stub would pass\" (§5). Correct: for each task's proofs, and each definition a proof reaches directly, run the proof against three stubs of that definition: (constantly nil), identity, and its first argument unchanged. A proof still green against a stub does not test that definition: a placebo, recorded as a problem fact (class :proof, naming the proof, the definition and the stub that passed). The stub is a real definition in a forked test environment holding exactly the definitions the run wants (never with-redefs or alter-var-root), on the fork path of `seon.agent/run-tests-forked`. Cost: proofs x directly reached definitions x 3 forked runs. The idea is writ's spec self-check, which rejects a law any implementation satisfies (notes/archive/option3-ECOSYSTEM.md; a first cut on jolt/patterns 35e1208). It would flag jolt/patterns' idiom proofs that exercised step-fns defined in the test file itself."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.program/definitions-from-the-compiler"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.proofs-test/a-proof-a-stub-passes-is-a-placebo seon.proofs-test/a-real-proof-fails-against-every-stub}}
 {:seon.task/name "names-are-clojures-words"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists (DECISIONS: Names are Clojure's, its libraries' or Jolt's; AGENTS.md §7a): pass 1 is merged. Old house words in names became Clojure's, a library's or Jolt's, by git mv and exact-token sed, one commit per word:
- door, entrance -> server: `seon.server` (`seon.server/ops`, a map of :op -> fn; error type :seon.server/defect); the MCP tools keep their seon_* names;
- verb -> function (by its var), or op where it is a request type;
- lane -> worktree session: bin/worktrees, bin/worktree-check (verdict WORKTREE-CHECK); `seon.fx`'s performer procs are workers (`seon.fx/worker-proc`);
- land, landing -> merge: docs/merging.md;
- dragon -> failure point: docs/failure-points.md; bin/laws lists the sites of four laws (catch, clocks, measures, resolution);
- census -> mg/check: `seon.check/mg-check`, bin/check mode mg-check;
- admit, guarantees (the contract sense) -> instrument: `seon.check/instrument`; `seon.fx/admit` is admission by workload and keeps its name;
- pillar -> principle; fence -> guard (a Markdown code fence, CommonMark's word, stays in `seon.reader` and `seon.ref`);
- merge train -> octopus merge (`seon.writer/octopus-merge`);
- harvest -> stage (`seon.stage/stage!`);
- stand-in -> proc (`seon.agent-proc`); the scripted model is \"the scripted model\";
- dial -> config key (`seon.reconcile/merge-limits`).
Stored names are pass 2 (`seon.db/stored-attributes-take-the-new-words`): task ids and task file names (seon.fences.edn, seon.entrance.edn, merge-trains-off-as-decided, the-dragon-gate-sees-fences, a-door-defect-answers-that-request-alone, a-train-is-proven-by-one-combined-run, with-merge-census-cost), `:seon.config.root/entrance-port`, `:seon.config.contract/guarantees`, `:seon.ai.model/thinking-dials`, and refusal with its stored keyword. waste stays `:seon.attempt/waste`; stuck goes with the budget (DECISIONS: Owner answers, 2026-10-23 morning). Archived notes keep their text. Proof that stays: `seon.docs-test/no-name-uses-an-old-word` reads AGENTS.md §7a's table and finds no namespace, var, check mode, bin script or docs page named with an old word (names from the compiler's facts, all-ns and ns-interns, not a regex over code; the kept senses listed in the test as data, each with its reason)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.docs-test/no-name-uses-an-old-word}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-help-page-shows-one-worked-turn"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: docs/agent.md (the system message, `seon.context/help-text`) teaches each function by a form but shows no worked example. SWE-agent without a demonstration lost 1.7 points; Manus warns that uniform few-shot patterns get copied, so show one example of the method and no template. Correct: one short, complete transcript in docs/agent.md#done: read a red proof, find the helper with `my.agent/callers`, redefine it in its namespace with a contract, `my.agent/prove` green, record the finding with `my.task/update!`. Its forms run in `seon.repl-test/the-help-page-runs`. It sits in the cached system message. Measure: turns to the first green proof and contract-gap refusals in first attempts."
  :seon.task/kind :work
